## 📌 Objective
Build a Machine Learning model to predict whether a person is at risk of **heart disease** based on health data.

---

## 📂 Dataset
| Property | Details |
|----------|---------|
| Source | Heart Disease UCI Dataset |
| Rows | 303 |
| Columns | 14 |
| Target | 0 = No Disease, 1 = Disease |

---

## 🛠️ Libraries Used
| Library | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| Pandas | Data loading and cleaning |
| NumPy | Numerical operations |
| Matplotlib & Seaborn | Visualization |
| Scikit-learn | ML models and evaluation |

---

## 📊 What Was Done
- Loaded and cleaned the dataset
- Checked for missing values (none found)
- Performed Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Visualized Age distribution, Box Plots, Correlation Heatmap
- Trained **Logistic Regression** model
- Trained **Decision Tree Classifier** model
- Evaluated using Accuracy, Confusion Matrix, ROC-AUC Curve
- Visualized Feature Importance (Decision Tree)

---

## 📈 Key Results
| Model | Accuracy | AUC Score |
|-------|----------|-----------|
| Logistic Regression | ~85% | ~0.91 |
| Decision Tree | ~80% | ~0.83 |

- ✅ Logistic Regression performed better overall
- ✅ Top features: **thalach**, **cp**, **oldpeak**
- ✅ No missing values found in dataset

---

## ▶️ How to Run

**Step 1:** Install libraries
```bash
